	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE D1:\nTwo TI ISO7741 (3 forward + 1 reverse channel each, 5 kVrms reinforced, SOIC-16 DW, output enables EN1/EN2). U43 = ISO7741F (default LOW): ENABLE, SCLK, MOSI. U44 = ISO7741 (default HIGH): CS_DAC, CS_ADC, CS_ADC2, MISO back. Six forward lines fit exactly; the CS lines sit on the default-HIGH part so nothing is selected and nothing drives MISO when the FPGA side is unpowered. Side 1 runs from +3V3_FPGA (J3 pin 1), side 2 from +3V3 [13]; both 2.25-5.5 V. One 100 nF at each VCC pin (C100-C103)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 53.34 193.04 0)
		(size 62 22)
		(margins 1 1 1 1)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "259bebb9-cf88-423c-abf2-d8fed84eef91")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE D2:\nDefault states with J3 unplugged or the FPGA unpowered: ISO_SCLK / ISO_MOSI / ISO_ENABLE LOW (PhotoMOS open), ISO_CS_DAC / ISO_CS_ADC / ISO_CS_ADC2 HIGH. EN1 / EN2 open = outputs enabled (internal pull-up, DS pin table). JP7 pulls both EN2 low for the J5 bypass; the side-1 outputs (MISO, FAULT_N) stay enabled, which is fine because J3 is then unplugged."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 53.34 217.17 0)
		(size 62 17)
		(margins 1 1 1 1)
		(stroke
			(width 0.8)
			(type solid)
			(color 200 200 200 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "Arial")
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9a709d2e-3f57-4445-a059-71313dd41072")
	)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE D3:\nSpare: U43 channel D, board -> FPGA, named FAULT_N. Board-side input ISO_FAULT_N is pulled up by R86 (idle = not faulted); the FPGA-side output goes to TP38 only, because J3 has no free pin (15 = CS_ADC2 since the two-ADC decision of 2026-11-08). Rev 2: J3 2x10 for FAULT_N and any PGOOD / OK lines."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
