	(text_box "MISC NOTE M1:\nBring-up: with JP7 OPEN and J3 unplugged, check ISO_ENABLE LOW (TP on [8]) and ISO_CS_* HIGH on J5. Then plug J3: FPGA toggles ENABLE, check ISO_ENABLE follows (DS 11 ns). Fallback if the SPI link misbehaves: JP7 CLOSED, ribbon on J5, FPGA drives the converters directly (3.3 V logic on both sides). Sourcing: ISO7741FDWR is LCSC / JLCPCB only today (DigiKey CA backorder); ISO7742FDWR (C2862403, DigiKey 3352 pcs) is the drop-in if it runs out: same footprint, 2 forward channels, so move SCLK to U44 and MISO to... no: keep U44 as drawn and use ISO7742F for ENABLE + MOSI only if SCLK can share U44's INC with GPIO moved to a jumper. Decide at order time."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
